<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="2,3-cis-flavanols biosynthesis" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260303222105">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-6035" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Arabidopsis thaliana col&lt;/i&gt;: The expected taxonomic range of the pathway includes Arabidopsis thaliana col, and, enzyme(s) that catalyzes one or more of the key reactions in this pathway were predicted in Arabidopsis thaliana col. &lt;A href=&quot;http://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; Flavonoids are highly diverse class of plant plant polyphenols (with about 9000 compounds have been identified so far |CITS: [16137727]| that impart much of the color and flavor of fruits and vegetables. They exhibit a wide range of biological functions in higher plants such as UV protection, flower coloration, and antimicrobial a activity |CITS: [11130659]|. They also exhibit antioxidant and anticancer properties |CITS: [12224601]| |CITS: [18645020]|. Flavan-3-ols, sometime referred to simply as flavanols, represent an important classs of flavonoids. They are the building blocks of condensed tannins, and exhibit numerous potentially benefical medicinal properties. They show antioxidant and free radical scavenging |CITS: [14733505]|, anticarcinogenic |CITS: [11448533]| and cardioprotective properties. It has recently been shown that epicatechin present in dark chocolate has the potential to promote cardiovascular health in humans . The most common flavan-3-ols belong to one of two sterioisofoms - either |FRAME: CPD-10359 &quot;(2&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;,3&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;)-flavan-3-ols&quot;| (2,3-&lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;-flavan-3-ols) or |FRAME: CPD-10414 &quot;(2&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;,3&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-flavan-3-ols&quot;| (2,3-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-flavan-3-ols).|FRAME: EC-1.3.1.77| converts anthocyanidins to their corresponding 2,3-&lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-flavan-3-ols.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE" />
    <Author name="karthik" />
  </Authors>
